  "interpretation": "Pure BAML expanded its allocator high-water mark during warmup but reached a clear plateau: checkpoints 4-10 changed only 0.047 MiB and fit 0.016 MiB/min while the managed heap returned to 15 runtime objects every time. Python BAML retained an upward post-GC trend despite both BAML major GC and CPython generation-2 GC: checkpoints 1-10 rose 5.578 MiB and fit 1.381 MiB/min. Its BAML managed heap had no cross-request live set at collection time, and CPython collected objects every cycle, so the retained Python-process RSS is outside the measured BAML heap. The five-minute run cannot by itself distinguish a native leak from allocator or runtime caches that plateau later."
